r=audit['release_query'];(OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text(f'''# Proprioceptive pose contract audit\n\nThe field called `proprio` is measured EEF pose only at initialization. Thereafter both training and inference intentionally use the previous absolute command target. This is a shared action-history contract, not a newly discovered measured-versus-commanded field mismatch.\n\n## Exact cached verification\n\nOriginal M6 reads `personal_demo_0001.npz`, selects 48 windows, and preserves the cached pose (except the M6 rotation-layout permutation). Selected window 10, RGB frame {frame}, starts at command {start}; its first 9 input fields exactly equal command {start-1}'s absolute target. All {len(errors)} noninitial cached frames have maximum difference 0.0. Full vectors and hashes are in `audit.json`.\n\nV4's actual `m7_catalog_data.pack` obtains the same source `proprio[frame]`, reorders rotations and zeroes placeholder grip fields. `m7_train.prepare` passes that vector directly to the model. Both the nominal writer (`scripts/m3_prepare_data.py:42-45`) and recovery collector (`m7_recovery.py:158-169`) explicitly insert the previous target. V4's broad M7 continuation is distinct from the old narrow M6 training set. The archived V4 source snapshot numeric check is not yet available locally.\n\n## Important implementation difference\n\nTraining `absolute_target` encodes the normalized expert/controller command against the current measured pose: measured position plus bounded translation, and bounded rotation relative to measured wrist. Inference `M7Policy.to_action` computes a bounded OSC command but then stores the raw model absolute target in its next pose-history input. Therefore a model prediction that is clipped or not physically achieved can be much farther from the actual wrist than a typical expert target. This is a distribution/feedback limitation even though the named contract agrees.\n\nAt film0006 release query 2, the archived input first 9 fields exactly equal raw predicted command 59. Raw input vs measured EEF: {r['raw_vs_actual_rotation_deg']:.4f}degrees and {r['raw_vs_actual_position_mm']:.4f}mm. Re-encoding the actual bounded command gives {r['bounded_vs_actual_rotation_deg']:.4f}degrees and {r['bounded_vs_actual_position_mm']:.4f}mm. Raw vs bounded target differs by {r['raw_vs_bounded_rotation_deg']:.4f}degrees and {r['raw_vs_bounded_position_mm']:.4f}mm.\n\nNo counterfactual output or physical success is implied. Substituting measured pose at inference would change the input contract; it needs a separately labelled sensitivity test and eventual training/evaluation qualification.\n\nReproduce: `.venv-sim/bin/python scripts/exp20261011_prompt_proprio_audit.py`.\n''');print(json.dumps(audit['release_query'],indent=2))

